  "details": "<p>This archive is located in the Nab<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0c1c18ae-7fff-5320-6d88-0d39b5a48d5d\"><span>\u00fb temple.</span></span></p>\r\n<p><span><span><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"453\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/DS-nabutemple1-2.png\" width=\"444\" /></span></span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Three tiers of niches were found in Room H 5 (on the northwestern side of Forecourt I) of the Nab\u00fb temple at Dur-\u0160arrukin, the short-lived capital of the Assyrian king Sargon II (721\u2013705 BC). Fragments of clay tablets and inscribed prisms in these niches suggest that a temple library was located here. The empty niches might be a result of the move of the capital to Nineveh under Sennacherib (704\u2013681 BC) or of the use of perishable writing materials.",
